<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Lyceum: third-party licenses</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: sans-serif; max-width: 60em; margin: 2em auto; padding: 0 1em; color: #222; background: #fff; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.6em; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.3em; margin-top: 2.5em; border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc; }
  h3 { font-size: 1.05em; margin-bottom: 0.3em; }
  ul.used-by { margin-top: 0; }
  pre.licence-text { white-space: pre-wrap; background: #f6f6f6; padding: 1em; border: 1px solid #ddd; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    body { color: #ddd; background: #161616; }
    pre.licence-text { background: #222; border-color: #333; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Lyceum: third-party licenses</h1>
<p>Lyceum's programs, the editor and the <code>lyceum</code> command, contain these third-party
Rust crates. Each license's text follows, with the crates it covers. Lyceum itself is licensed
under the MIT license (<code>LICENSE</code>); <code>NOTICE.txt</code> names its source and its
other attributions.</p>
<!-- licences -->
<h3>Overview</h3>
<ul class="overview">
{{#each overview}}
  <li>{{name}} ({{count}})</li>
{{/each}}
</ul>
{{#each licenses}}
<div class="licence">
  <h3 id="{{id}}">{{name}}</h3>
  <p>Used by:</p>
  <ul class="used-by">
  {{#each used_by}}
    <li>{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}{{#if crate.repository}} (<a href="{{crate.repository}}">{{crate.repository}}</a>){{/if}}</li>
  {{/each}}
  </ul>
  <pre class="licence-text">{{text}}</pre>
</div>
{{/each}}
<!-- /licences -->
</body>
</html>
